WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.417 --> 00:00:04.917 line:5%,start
[Vision] <i>It's been years.</i>
<i>I'm just not very good with people.</i>

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.333 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] <i>Accessing previous files</i>
<i>relating to program VisionQuest.</i>

3
00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:09.750 line:95%,end
Welcome home, Vision.

4
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:11.167 line:95%,end
So, you were smiling today,

5
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.250 line:95%,end
-which is good.
-Mmm-hmm.

6
00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:14.583 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] Miss Edith.

7
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:18.333 line:95%,end
This house is architecturally
and emotionally unstable.

8
00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.375 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>Well, he knows</i>
<i>the facts of his old life.</i>

9
00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:22.167 line:95%,end
<i>Now, he's searching for the feeling of it.</i>

10
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.083 line:95%,end
You're a ghost, haunting her footsteps.

11
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:26.750 line:95%,end
Not her footsteps, his.

12
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:29.667 line:95%,end
<i>I wish to understand him</i>
<i>and how he existed in this world.</i>

13
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.625 line:95%,end
[Vision] You're familiar with the thought
experiment the Ship of Theseus?

14
00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:35.208 line:95%,end
-Naturally.
-When no original plank remains,

15
00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:37.833 line:95%,end
is it still the Ship of Theseus?

16
00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:41.917 line:95%,end
Both are the true ship.

17
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.542 line:95%,end
Someone out there placed a sizeable bounty
on Vision's AI-infested head.

18
00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:51.083 line:95%,end
Hey V, skylight exit?

19
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.958 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>And the contract</i>
<i>went to a hunter,</i>

20
00:00:53.042 --> 00:00:55.000 line:95%,end
<i>known only as "the Paladin".</i>

21
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.917 line:95%,end
-[Paladin] What do you got?
-He has a family.

22
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.375 line:95%,end
Had. Twin boys, Billy and Tommy.

23
00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:04.083 line:95%,end
[reporter] <i>Thought deceased for years</i>

24
00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:07.250 line:95%,end
<i>The Vision has suddenly</i>
<i>and violently reappeared.</i>

25
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.333 line:95%,end
You're right.

26
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:10.625 line:95%,end
-You're name's Thomas Shepherd.
-Is it?

27
00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:13.958 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Take a look at this, police</i>
<i>psych evaluation and incident report,</i>

28
00:01:14.042 --> 00:01:15.083 line:95%,end
<i>London.</i>

29
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.292 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>This is not a test.</i>

30
00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:21.000 line:95%,end
<i>I am the emergency.</i>

31
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.083 line:95%,end
I have your son.

32
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.792 line:95%,end
[Thomas shudders] <i>I had a family,</i>

33
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:29.333 line:95%,end
<i>and parents that weren't my parents.</i>

34
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.333 line:95%,end
<i>A mother, he called her Wanda.</i>

35
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:33.667 line:95%,end
<i>And a father-- she called him Vision.</i>

36
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.167 line:95%,end
<i>Mazel tov!</i> It's a boy.

37
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.583 line:5%,start
<i>Yeah, I was at the pool.</i>
<i>Kids were havin' a laugh, holding me under</i>

38
00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:55.667 line:95%,end
<i>but for too long.</i>

39
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.083 line:5%,start
[chuckles] <i>Then it was like a...</i>

40
00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:06.542 line:5%,start
[breathing heavily]
<i>Like a bolt of lightning.</i>

41
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:09.917 line:95%,end
<i>And then, and then...</i> [shudders]

42
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.875 line:95%,end
<i>And then I wasn't just me anymore.</i>

43
00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:13.667 line:95%,end
Uh... [shudders]

44
00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.625 line:95%,end
<i>I was... I was someone else.</i>

45
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.042 line:95%,end
<i>Like, someone else had just moved</i>
<i>into my brain with me.</i>

46
00:02:20.125 --> 00:02:23.125 line:95%,end
<i>How can it feel so real?</i>

47
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:25.542 line:95%,end
<i>When I know it's impossible!</i>

48
00:02:25.625 --> 00:02:28.000 line:95%,end
<i>How can I have two lives?</i>

49
00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:29.500 line:95%,end
<i>Please!</i>

50
00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:31.375 line:95%,end
[doctor] <i>How long has he been saying this?</i>

51
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:32.458 line:95%,end
[police constable] <i>Six months.</i>

52
00:02:33.208 --> 00:02:35.708 line:95%,end
[doctor] <i>Done all we can for him here.</i>
<i>Take him to transport.</i>

53
00:02:35.792 --> 00:02:37.875 line:5%,start
<i>I'm not crazy. I'm not crazy, I'm not.</i>

54
00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:40.458 line:5%,start
<i>I'm not. You have to believe me! Please!</i>

55
00:02:40.542 --> 00:02:42.000 line:95%,end
[loud buzz]

56
00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:59.250 line:95%,end
[court transport official] <i>Loading up</i>
<i>young offenders</i>

57
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:01.000 line:95%,end
<i>for court services transfer.</i>

58
00:03:01.417 --> 00:03:04.083 line:95%,end
I do not care what your story is,

59
00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.458 line:95%,end
what your meds are, what you're in for.

60
00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:08.708 line:95%,end
Couldn't give a shit
if you're Oliver Twist,

61
00:03:08.792 --> 00:03:12.750 line:95%,end
Hannibal Lecter or if you are the sort
that wouldn't harm a fly!

62
00:03:13.875 --> 00:03:15.083 line:95%,end
Let's keep moving, son.
What are you waiting for?

63
00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:16.583 line:95%,end
It's not a parade. Let's go!

64
00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:19.292 line:95%,end
Come on. Move along now. This is my bus,

65
00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:23.000 line:95%,end
and the sooner you understand that,
the better we are all gonna get along.

66
00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:24.375 line:95%,end
Okay?

67
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:25.583 line:95%,end
Don't eyeball me, son.

68
00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:27.667 line:95%,end
That is not my issue!

69
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.958 line:95%,end
[Lisa] This seat taken?

70
00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:31.458 line:95%,end
Well, it is now.

71
00:03:32.458 --> 00:03:34.500 line:95%,end
[Clancy] Sorry about the bracelets,
but I have to say,

72
00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:36.708 line:95%,end
it's better for you
and it's better for me.

73
00:03:36.792 --> 00:03:40.333 line:95%,end
-First time?
-We have got a long drive,

74
00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:42.875 line:95%,end
and I have got a short fuse.

75
00:03:42.958 --> 00:03:45.875 line:95%,end
So, choose your seatmates carefully,

76
00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:49.167 line:95%,end
and keep your mouths shut.

77
00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.667 line:95%,end
[taser crackling]

78
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.083 line:95%,end
[breathes deeply]

79
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:53.917 line:95%,end
And have yourself

80
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.583 line:95%,end
a merry little Christmas.

81
00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.708 line:95%,end
[♪ pop rock music playing,
The Hep Stars "Christmas On My Mind"]

82
00:03:58.792 --> 00:04:01.875 line:5%,start
♪<i> I've got Christmas on my mind </i>♪

83
00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:06.125 line:95%,end
♪ <i>I adore that lovely time </i>♪

84
00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:11.250 line:95%,end
♪<i> I'm feeling like I was a little child </i>♪

85
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:14.958 line:95%,end
♪ <i>When I've got Christmas on my mind </i>♪

86
00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:17.250 line:95%,end
So, what's your...

87
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.250 line:95%,end
name?

88
00:04:20.583 --> 00:04:24.083 line:95%,end
♪ <i>I wonder how I've been this year </i>♪

89
00:04:25.125 --> 00:04:28.417 line:95%,end
♪ <i>If I've been nice Santa comes to me </i>♪

90
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.792 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Oh, I've got Christmas on my mind </i>♪

91
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.500 line:95%,end
[Young Billy and Tommy scream]

92
00:04:34.583 --> 00:04:36.250 line:95%,end
[tattooed man] I swear, I said,
I'm not going back!

93
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:39.333 line:95%,end
I'm not going back.
No, no. This ain't the way.

94
00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:41.333 line:95%,end
I'm not going back. I'm not. No!
[whimpers]

95
00:04:41.417 --> 00:04:43.083 line:95%,end
Not where we're going. [shuddering]

96
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:46.375 line:95%,end
I'm not going back, I said--
I swear, I said, I'm not going back!

97
00:04:46.458 --> 00:04:47.542 line:95%,end
No, no!

98
00:04:47.625 --> 00:04:50.208 line:95%,end
-[shuddering]
-[Lisa] Look at me.

99
00:04:50.917 --> 00:04:52.292 line:95%,end
Take a breath.

100
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.333 line:95%,end
Yeah, I'm trying.

101
00:04:57.042 --> 00:04:58.042 line:95%,end
Look at me.

102
00:04:58.125 --> 00:04:59.125 line:95%,end
[shuddering]

103
00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:00.833 line:95%,end
Look at me!

104
00:05:01.833 --> 00:05:03.708 line:95%,end
Friendly bet, I can guess your story.

105
00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:06.333 line:95%,end
Couple of scrapes.

106
00:05:07.292 --> 00:05:08.958 line:95%,end
Seen your fair share of dust-ups?

107
00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:13.042 line:95%,end
Maybe, the back of a police car
once or twice,

108
00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:15.208 line:95%,end
but never like this.

109
00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:18.167 line:95%,end
You forgot dead mum, dead-beat dad--

110
00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.750 line:95%,end
Right, definitely no family to speak of.

111
00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.292 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Just a trail of fosters,

112
00:05:22.375 --> 00:05:23.917 line:95%,end
and they all leave.

113
00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:26.375 line:95%,end
Orphaned once...

114
00:05:27.375 --> 00:05:28.958 line:95%,end
Orphaned twice and so on.

115
00:05:29.042 --> 00:05:30.417 line:95%,end
And so forth.

116
00:05:33.542 --> 00:05:35.083 line:95%,end
Yeah.

117
00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:36.333 line:95%,end
Right.

118
00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.042 line:95%,end
In my experience,

119
00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:44.792 line:95%,end
who you are is less important
than who you pretend to be.

120
00:05:44.875 --> 00:05:46.208 line:95%,end
And who should that be?

121
00:05:46.292 --> 00:05:48.333 line:95%,end
[scoffs] Whoever keeps you alive.

122
00:05:49.833 --> 00:05:51.208 line:95%,end
'Ell...

123
00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:54.833 line:95%,end
each mornin' is a chance to become...

124
00:05:55.708 --> 00:05:56.917 line:95%,end
someone new.

125
00:06:00.375 --> 00:06:01.417 line:95%,end
Who I am is a bit...

126
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:02.500 line:95%,end
Tommy!

127
00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:04.083 line:95%,end
-[Young Tommy screams]
-Vision cries]

128
00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:05.167 line:95%,end
Tommy.

129
00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.250 line:95%,end
in flux...

130
00:06:07.792 --> 00:06:08.792 line:95%,end
these days.

131
00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:14.417 line:95%,end
Well... enough pretend.

132
00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.250 line:95%,end
What got you here?

133
00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:19.958 line:95%,end
[chuckles softly]

134
00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:22.625 line:95%,end
Just a...

135
00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:26.042 line:95%,end
teeny-tiny psychotic break.

136
00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:28.625 line:95%,end
What about you?

137
00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:32.833 line:95%,end
I killed a man and then wore his face
to escape capture.

138
00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:34.458 line:95%,end
[chuckles]

139
00:06:36.042 --> 00:06:37.542 line:95%,end
Minor larceny.

140
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.542 line:95%,end
Compulsive kleptomania.

141
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.750 line:95%,end
I'm a pickpocket.

142
00:06:44.083 --> 00:06:46.583 line:95%,end
Damn, damn good one, actually.

143
00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:50.125 line:95%,end
I'm guessing you're a better picker
than chooser of pockets.

144
00:06:50.208 --> 00:06:53.083 line:95%,end
Uh, to be fair,
I lifted the wallet clean up

145
00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.750 line:95%,end
-before I even noticed the badge. So...
-[chuckles]

146
00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:57.375 line:95%,end
Thank you very much.

147
00:06:57.458 --> 00:06:58.458 line:95%,end
Nice.

148
00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.292 line:95%,end
There was this one time, Cardiff town,

149
00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:04.500 line:95%,end
five men, six wallets,

150
00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:06.375 line:95%,end
and two kebabs by the end of the night.

151
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.833 line:95%,end
[tattooed man] Swear, I said,
I'm not going back!

152
00:07:14.917 --> 00:07:16.708 line:95%,end
No, I'm not. I'm not going back.

153
00:07:16.792 --> 00:07:19.375 line:95%,end
Not where we're going. I swear--
I'm not going back.

154
00:07:19.458 --> 00:07:22.167 line:95%,end
Not where we're going,
I swear, I said, I'm not going back!

155
00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.208 line:95%,end
No, no. I'm not going back.

156
00:07:24.292 --> 00:07:25.292 line:95%,end
-[male inmate 1] Shut up!
-[tattooed man] I swear!

157
00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:26.667 line:95%,end
I'm not-- I'm not going back!

158
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.750 line:95%,end
-Hey, mate... Shh. put a lid on it.
-[male inmate 2] Keep it down.

159
00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:32.417 line:95%,end
-[male inmate 3] Wasteman.
-Look, we're only going to a local nick.

160
00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.542 line:95%,end
[Clancy laughs]

161
00:07:35.792 --> 00:07:39.917 line:95%,end
Do you honestly believe
that we are heading for Young Offenders?

162
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.500 line:95%,end
Or the big kids' pen?

163
00:07:42.583 --> 00:07:45.833 line:95%,end
The court has deemed
your new home elsewhere.

164
00:07:45.917 --> 00:07:48.542 line:95%,end
-[female inmate 1] Are you serious?
-And there's no parole.

165
00:07:48.625 --> 00:07:49.833 line:95%,end
There's no sun.

166
00:07:49.917 --> 00:07:53.417 line:95%,end
And there's no forgetting
to take your meds.

167
00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:56.958 line:95%,end
The next stop for this bus
is the lovely chateau of Saint Mabyn's.

168
00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:58.167 line:95%,end
[male inmate 5] Yo, nah, brother.

169
00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.500 line:95%,end
[male inmate 5] Are you quite serious?

170
00:07:59.583 --> 00:08:02.000 line:95%,end
-What's that?
-A sanitarium.

171
00:08:02.083 --> 00:08:03.750 line:95%,end
[tattooed man]
No, no, no. I'm not going back.

172
00:08:03.833 --> 00:08:06.000 line:95%,end
I'm not going back. I'm not, I'm not--

173
00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:07.333 line:95%,end
-[tasing]
-[tattooed man screaming]

174
00:08:07.417 --> 00:08:08.417 line:95%,end
[groaning]

175
00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:13.375 line:95%,end
All right, that's enough!
You're hurting him!

176
00:08:13.458 --> 00:08:16.458 line:95%,end
Now you hush up and you take your seat.

177
00:08:16.542 --> 00:08:19.583 line:95%,end
We can't go to Saint Mabyn's.
No one ever gets out of it!

178
00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:20.875 line:95%,end
I said, be quiet--

179
00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:22.667 line:95%,end
No, no, no. Please, please, please.
Come on, don't.

180
00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.667 line:95%,end
-[tasing]
-[Thomas screaming]

181
00:08:25.417 --> 00:08:27.042 line:95%,end
[groaning]

182
00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:35.083 line:95%,end
[screaming]

183
00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:37.042 line:95%,end
[groans]

184
00:08:37.125 --> 00:08:38.292 line:95%,end
[panting]

185
00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:41.833 line:95%,end
[Clancy] Okay...

186
00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.792 line:95%,end
Anyone makes another sound,
leaves here on a stretcher.

187
00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.333 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

188
00:08:51.583 --> 00:08:53.583 line:95%,end
What's wrong with this bloody thing?

189
00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.667 line:95%,end
[panting]

190
00:08:58.958 --> 00:09:00.333 line:95%,end
What the hell was that?

191
00:09:00.417 --> 00:09:02.042 line:95%,end
[both panting]

192
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:04.458 line:95%,end
-A Christmas miracle?
-I don't think so.

193
00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:07.875 line:95%,end
But this is.

194
00:09:08.458 --> 00:09:09.958 line:95%,end
There's an exit door in the back.

195
00:09:11.792 --> 00:09:14.917 line:95%,end
You want me to jump out of a moving bus?
Well, that's suicide.

196
00:09:15.625 --> 00:09:17.500 line:95%,end
So is where we're going.

197
00:09:22.917 --> 00:09:25.958 line:95%,end
-You ready, spark plug?
-Too soon.

198
00:09:26.042 --> 00:09:27.667 line:95%,end
[panting]

199
00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.917 line:95%,end
-[Clancy] Hey!
-[Thomas] Go, go, go.

200
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.458 line:95%,end
[Clancy] Hey! No! No! No! No!

201
00:09:35.542 --> 00:09:37.042 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Go, go, go, go, go, go, go.

202
00:09:37.542 --> 00:09:39.333 line:95%,end
[laughing]

203
00:09:40.958 --> 00:09:42.667 line:95%,end
Oh, look, he's got a spare.

204
00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.125 line:95%,end
-Shit. Get the door!
-[Clancy laughs]

205
00:09:45.542 --> 00:09:47.125 line:95%,end
[Thomas panting]

206
00:09:47.208 --> 00:09:48.583 line:95%,end
Stop the bus!

207
00:09:48.667 --> 00:09:51.042 line:95%,end
[Clancy] You messed with the wrong guard!

208
00:09:51.792 --> 00:09:53.792 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Dashing through the snow </i>♪

209
00:09:53.875 --> 00:09:56.417 line:95%,end
♪ <i>In a one-horse open sleigh... </i>♪

210
00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.375 line:95%,end
Stop the bus!

211
00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:00.667 line:95%,end
♪ <i>...Laughing all the way </i>♪

212
00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.542 line:95%,end
Get out of there!

213
00:10:02.625 --> 00:10:04.833 line:95%,end
-They key won't work.
-Let me try.

214
00:10:04.917 --> 00:10:07.042 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Bells on bobtails ring... </i>♪

215
00:10:07.125 --> 00:10:09.000 line:95%,end
Stop singing!

216
00:10:09.083 --> 00:10:10.583 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Oh, what fun it is to ride... </i>♪

217
00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:11.917 line:95%,end
Oh, come on!

218
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.833 line:95%,end
Stop this singing!

219
00:10:13.917 --> 00:10:16.417 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Jingle bells, jingle all the way... </i>♪

220
00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.250 line:95%,end
[grunting]

221
00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.208 line:95%,end
[grunting loudly]

222
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.500 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Jingle bells, jingle bells,</i>
<i>jingle all the way </i>♪

223
00:10:27.375 --> 00:10:28.833 line:95%,end
[Lisa screams]

224
00:10:28.958 --> 00:10:31.333 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Hey! Jingle bells, jingle bells... </i>♪

225
00:10:32.042 --> 00:10:34.125 line:95%,end
[panting]

226
00:10:36.375 --> 00:10:38.708 line:95%,end
-Lisa.
-Tommy.

227
00:10:38.792 --> 00:10:40.625 line:95%,end
Thomas. My name's Thomas.

228
00:10:40.708 --> 00:10:42.875 line:95%,end
Well, Thomas, run!

229
00:10:42.958 --> 00:10:44.250 line:95%,end
[both chuckle]

230
00:11:16.917 --> 00:11:19.333 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>What is happening</i>
<i>to your world, Vision?</i>

231
00:11:19.417 --> 00:11:20.750 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] <i>It's a signal of some kind.</i>

232
00:11:20.833 --> 00:11:23.875 line:95%,end
<i>I'd have to bypass our security</i>
<i>protocols in order to access it.</i>

233
00:11:23.958 --> 00:11:25.917 line:95%,end
-[Friday] <i>Vision, what are you doing?</i>
-[Vision] <i>I'm curious.</i>

234
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.208 line:95%,end
-[Jarvis] <i>You're reckless.</i>
-[Thomas] <i>I had a family.</i>

235
00:11:28.292 --> 00:11:30.917 line:95%,end
<i>Um, a mother, he called her Wanda.</i>

236
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.875 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>I'm not made of Vibranium.</i>

237
00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:35.917 line:95%,end
<i>I don't phase, and I can't shoot lasers.</i>

238
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.917 line:95%,end
-[Thomas] <i>And a father...</i>
-[Paladin] <i>But I got something better...</i>

239
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.125 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>She called him Vision.</i>

240
00:11:40.208 --> 00:11:41.667 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>I have your son.</i>

241
00:11:45.458 --> 00:11:47.000 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>I don't know</i>
<i>what's happening to me.</i>

242
00:11:47.083 --> 00:11:51.625 line:95%,end
[shuddering] <i>Okay, but...</i>
<i>But I know it's true.</i>

243
00:11:51.708 --> 00:11:52.708 line:95%,end
<i>It's true.</i>

244
00:11:54.667 --> 00:11:56.500 line:95%,end
This was you.

245
00:11:56.583 --> 00:11:58.458 line:95%,end
I would be the first to warn you,

246
00:11:58.542 --> 00:12:02.042 line:95%,end
never leave me unsupervised
around a box of dynamite.

247
00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:04.875 line:95%,end
But you've left me here
without even a fuse.

248
00:12:04.958 --> 00:12:09.542 line:95%,end
No, the bounty hunter's voice,
booming out of the sky was not me.

249
00:12:09.625 --> 00:12:12.500 line:95%,end
Don't equivocate.
It's the consequence of you!

250
00:12:12.583 --> 00:12:16.542 line:95%,end
It's the consequence of a world
that's finally come knocking.

251
00:12:16.625 --> 00:12:20.583 line:95%,end
And quite frankly a tremendous opportunity
for you to branch out.

252
00:12:20.667 --> 00:12:22.292 line:95%,end
Network, meet a new friend.

253
00:12:22.375 --> 00:12:25.875 line:95%,end
Oh, this bounty hunter who so impossibly
claims to have my son?

254
00:12:25.958 --> 00:12:27.333 line:95%,end
-Is it?
-Is it what?

255
00:12:27.417 --> 00:12:29.458 line:95%,end
Really that impossible?

256
00:12:29.542 --> 00:12:32.167 line:95%,end
You should know by now,
this universe of theirs

257
00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.042 line:95%,end
is a very strange one.

258
00:12:41.875 --> 00:12:44.000 line:95%,end
So tell me, what do we know
about this Paladin?

259
00:12:44.083 --> 00:12:46.542 line:95%,end
This isn't any old shagger
with a dog and a shotgun.

260
00:12:49.583 --> 00:12:52.417 line:95%,end
Paladin is last in a centuries-long
line of hunters.

261
00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.500 line:95%,end
He's not The Paladin.

262
00:12:54.583 --> 00:12:56.875 line:95%,end
He's a Paladin.

263
00:12:57.792 --> 00:12:59.167 line:95%,end
Generation after generation,

264
00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.958 line:95%,end
chasing down his targets
for the highest bidder.

265
00:13:02.042 --> 00:13:03.958 line:95%,end
The sharpest of minds,

266
00:13:04.042 --> 00:13:06.542 line:95%,end
trained in every art and every weapon.

267
00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.375 line:95%,end
Good, bad--

268
00:13:09.458 --> 00:13:10.667 line:95%,end
Hero, villain.

269
00:13:11.375 --> 00:13:12.625 line:95%,end
He doesn't discriminate.

270
00:13:13.208 --> 00:13:17.042 line:95%,end
He'll find you,
bring you in alive per the contract,

271
00:13:17.125 --> 00:13:19.417 line:95%,end
or dead if you get in his way.

272
00:13:23.167 --> 00:13:26.792 line:95%,end
And he does all of it
believing himself to be righteous.

273
00:13:29.583 --> 00:13:32.750 line:95%,end
Simply put, he's a bounty hunter.

274
00:13:33.208 --> 00:13:35.250 line:95%,end
Once he's accepted a target,

275
00:13:35.333 --> 00:13:38.250 line:95%,end
he's bound by an unbreakable contract,

276
00:13:38.333 --> 00:13:41.042 line:95%,end
and his new target is you.

277
00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:54.667 line:95%,end
[Thomas panting]

278
00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.042 line:95%,end
-Welcome home, kid.
-[Thomas] No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

279
00:13:57.125 --> 00:13:59.708 line:95%,end
-I swear, I swear. I don't belong here.
-[alarm blaring]

280
00:14:01.833 --> 00:14:04.250 line:95%,end
Hey. Hey, look, I don't know
what you want from me,

281
00:14:04.333 --> 00:14:07.333 line:95%,end
but, you don't need to do this, okay?
I swear, I'm not dangerous.

282
00:14:07.417 --> 00:14:09.292 line:95%,end
You can't leave me here, please! Please!

283
00:14:09.375 --> 00:14:10.667 line:95%,end
-[Clancy] Is that you?
-Please!

284
00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.375 line:95%,end
[Clancy] Cannot stand here,
you cause havoc.

285
00:14:14.125 --> 00:14:15.583 line:95%,end
You.

286
00:14:15.667 --> 00:14:18.792 line:95%,end
Jingle bells, I knew I'd see you again.

287
00:14:20.208 --> 00:14:22.208 line:95%,end
Okay, I don't know who you people are,

288
00:14:22.292 --> 00:14:25.250 line:95%,end
but you just made a big mistake.

289
00:14:26.583 --> 00:14:27.792 line:95%,end
-[tasing]
-[screams]

290
00:14:27.875 --> 00:14:28.917 line:95%,end
[gunshot fired]

291
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.500 line:95%,end
[shuddering]

292
00:14:34.125 --> 00:14:35.417 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring]

293
00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:37.750 line:95%,end
Why did you do that?

294
00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.458 line:95%,end
You're mental.

295
00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.542 line:95%,end
You can't leave me here, please. Please!

296
00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.125 line:95%,end
I've got something, sir.

297
00:14:51.208 --> 00:14:53.000 line:95%,end
This is a recording made a year ago.

298
00:14:53.083 --> 00:14:56.042 line:95%,end
It appears a handful of teens
were injured at a swimming pool,

299
00:14:56.125 --> 00:14:57.542 line:95%,end
and this boy was held responsible.

300
00:14:57.625 --> 00:14:58.792 line:95%,end
He was arrested,

301
00:14:58.875 --> 00:15:00.792 line:95%,end
and taken for this psychiatric evaluation.

302
00:15:00.875 --> 00:15:03.667 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>I was myself and then I wasn't.</i>

303
00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.000 line:95%,end
<i>I have these memories of...</i>

304
00:15:06.875 --> 00:15:08.792 line:95%,end
<i>of someone I'm not, but...</i>

305
00:15:08.875 --> 00:15:10.333 line:95%,end
[shuddering]

306
00:15:11.125 --> 00:15:12.125 line:95%,end
<i>Now I</i>

307
00:15:12.208 --> 00:15:13.208 line:95%,end
<i>am</i>

308
00:15:13.292 --> 00:15:14.292 line:95%,end
<i>also...</i>

309
00:15:14.375 --> 00:15:16.083 line:95%,end
[doctor] <i>Memories of what?</i>

310
00:15:16.167 --> 00:15:20.292 line:95%,end
<i>Uh, a house, only haunted.</i>

311
00:15:21.542 --> 00:15:24.458 line:95%,end
<i>Like, the air itself was having a laugh.</i>

312
00:15:24.542 --> 00:15:26.458 line:95%,end
<i>Like an audience that wasn't there.</i>

313
00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.250 line:95%,end
<i>And there were meatloaves.</i>

314
00:15:31.458 --> 00:15:33.167 line:95%,end
<i>And green lawns.</i>

315
00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.083 line:95%,end
<i>Pixelated almost.</i>

316
00:15:35.625 --> 00:15:37.000 line:95%,end
[Thomas shuddering]

317
00:15:38.167 --> 00:15:41.042 line:95%,end
[Wanda] <i>Don't you want to meet</i>
<i>your son as yourself?</i>

318
00:15:42.625 --> 00:15:44.458 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>There was a man.</i>

319
00:15:44.542 --> 00:15:47.042 line:95%,end
<i>His face like...</i> [shudders]

320
00:15:47.125 --> 00:15:48.417 line:95%,end
<i>Like a demon.</i>

321
00:15:50.083 --> 00:15:51.333 line:95%,end
<i>Blood red.</i>

322
00:15:52.708 --> 00:15:55.917 line:95%,end
[stutters] <i>Like a... deep purple bruise</i>

323
00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:59.167 line:95%,end
but with these kind eyes.

324
00:16:00.583 --> 00:16:01.708 line:95%,end
<i>He wasn't human.</i>

325
00:16:03.458 --> 00:16:05.375 line:95%,end
<i>But he called me son.</i>

326
00:16:05.917 --> 00:16:07.000 line:95%,end
[video stops]

327
00:16:13.083 --> 00:16:14.208 line:95%,end
Okay.

328
00:16:15.875 --> 00:16:18.583 line:95%,end
The bounty hunter seems to be suggesting

329
00:16:18.667 --> 00:16:22.667 line:95%,end
that your offspring, somehow,

330
00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:26.375 line:95%,end
escaped from Wanda Maximoff's
witchy bubble.

331
00:16:26.458 --> 00:16:28.125 line:95%,end
Which of course, is impossible.

332
00:16:28.208 --> 00:16:29.708 line:95%,end
See, there's that word again.

333
00:16:29.792 --> 00:16:33.750 line:95%,end
When Wanda ended her Westview fantasy,
no entity she conjured survived.

334
00:16:33.833 --> 00:16:37.875 line:95%,end
You really believe this is
a sort of tactical deception?

335
00:16:37.958 --> 00:16:42.292 line:95%,end
Yes, I do. I do. I think
it's a sentimental ploy to draw me out.

336
00:16:42.375 --> 00:16:43.500 line:95%,end
Draw you out for whom?

337
00:16:45.167 --> 00:16:47.292 line:95%,end
Someone hired Paladin.

338
00:16:47.375 --> 00:16:48.583 line:95%,end
Could be S.W.O.R.D.

339
00:16:50.958 --> 00:16:53.875 line:95%,end
When they rebuilt you,
they turned you into a weapon.

340
00:16:54.708 --> 00:16:56.292 line:95%,end
Now they want it back.

341
00:16:59.125 --> 00:17:00.917 line:95%,end
There's something else you need to see.

342
00:17:02.208 --> 00:17:04.000 line:95%,end
-[doctor] <i>About your mother...</i>
-[Thomas] <i>Wanda.</i>

343
00:17:04.083 --> 00:17:05.917 line:95%,end
<i>Yeah, yeah. Um...</i>

344
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.167 line:95%,end
<i>She sings me songs.</i>

345
00:17:09.125 --> 00:17:10.750 line:95%,end
<i>Reads me stories.</i>

346
00:17:10.833 --> 00:17:12.417 line:95%,end
<i>But her...</i>

347
00:17:13.625 --> 00:17:14.625 line:95%,end
<i>Her eyes,</i>

348
00:17:16.208 --> 00:17:17.208 line:95%,end
<i>sad.</i>

349
00:17:19.333 --> 00:17:22.333 line:95%,end
<i>She had too much feeling.</i> [shudders]

350
00:17:23.208 --> 00:17:25.125 line:95%,end
<i>Too much love...</i>

351
00:17:26.625 --> 00:17:28.708 line:95%,end
<i>and so much pain.</i>

352
00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.250 line:95%,end
<i>Loss.</i>

353
00:17:31.667 --> 00:17:33.000 line:95%,end
<i>Our dog died.</i>

354
00:17:34.708 --> 00:17:36.583 line:95%,end
<i>But I never had a dog.</i>

355
00:17:36.667 --> 00:17:38.500 line:95%,end
<i>But I did, I did.</i>

356
00:17:40.125 --> 00:17:41.125 line:95%,end
<i>Uh, she...</i>

357
00:17:42.333 --> 00:17:44.625 line:95%,end
<i>She said a thing to make it all right.</i>

358
00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:51.458 line:95%,end
"Grief is just love persevering."

359
00:17:55.375 --> 00:17:57.125 line:95%,end
[doctor] <i>Could it be</i>
<i>that you imagined her?</i>

360
00:17:57.208 --> 00:18:00.417 line:95%,end
<i>An orphan that wanted</i>
<i>a loving family so deeply</i>

361
00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.875 line:95%,end
<i>that he conjured one of his own?</i>

362
00:18:01.958 --> 00:18:04.042 line:95%,end
<i>No! 'Cause I know it's not real, okay?</i>

363
00:18:04.125 --> 00:18:06.458 line:95%,end
<i>I know it's not real! But it feels real!</i>

364
00:18:06.542 --> 00:18:11.000 line:95%,end
<i>Yes, like my mother wasn't a witch</i>
<i>and my father wasn't a machine.</i>

365
00:18:11.083 --> 00:18:14.292 line:95%,end
<i>Please help me!</i>
<i>Please, I don't know who I am!</i>

366
00:18:14.375 --> 00:18:16.250 line:95%,end
<i>I don't know who I am.</i>

367
00:18:16.333 --> 00:18:17.333 line:95%,end
[snaps fingers]

368
00:18:20.083 --> 00:18:22.667 line:95%,end
There were only two people
in the room when you...

369
00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:25.125 line:95%,end
when he, the original Vision
said that to Wanda.

370
00:18:25.708 --> 00:18:28.042 line:95%,end
This boy couldn't possible know that.

371
00:18:28.125 --> 00:18:29.417 line:95%,end
And yet he does.

372
00:18:32.667 --> 00:18:35.542 line:95%,end
Sir, I found coordinates
embedded in Paladin's message.

373
00:18:39.417 --> 00:18:41.250 line:95%,end
It's an invitation.

374
00:19:23.292 --> 00:19:24.958 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Oh, look at you.

375
00:19:26.125 --> 00:19:29.125 line:95%,end
Walking around like you're people.

376
00:19:29.208 --> 00:19:32.000 line:95%,end
Is that like a holo-projection thing?

377
00:19:35.125 --> 00:19:37.958 line:95%,end
Okay. I'd offer you a drink,

378
00:19:38.042 --> 00:19:40.792 line:95%,end
but according to your technical specs,

379
00:19:40.875 --> 00:19:43.542 line:95%,end
you can't. Right?

380
00:19:43.625 --> 00:19:45.583 line:95%,end
Churns the guts.

381
00:19:45.667 --> 00:19:46.958 line:95%,end
[in robotic voice] Excruciating.

382
00:19:48.375 --> 00:19:51.292 line:95%,end
[in normal voice] If I'm honest,
the older I get, same.

383
00:19:52.417 --> 00:19:55.167 line:95%,end
Everybody bleeds underneath.

384
00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.750 line:95%,end
My point is...

385
00:19:57.708 --> 00:19:59.333 line:95%,end
[both] You're as human as the rest of us.

386
00:19:59.417 --> 00:20:01.042 line:95%,end
-Everything dies.
-Everything dies.

387
00:20:01.917 --> 00:20:03.083 line:95%,end
Including you.

388
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.000 line:95%,end
Yes.

389
00:20:05.958 --> 00:20:08.958 line:95%,end
You see, I've already sat through
a quintillion simulations

390
00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:10.708 line:95%,end
of this very conversation.

391
00:20:10.792 --> 00:20:14.625 line:95%,end
I've computed every conceivable
combination of words you might use,

392
00:20:14.708 --> 00:20:16.750 line:95%,end
actions you might take.

393
00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.625 line:95%,end
I can't be throw off-balance by this...

394
00:20:20.583 --> 00:20:22.833 line:95%,end
guileless manipulation.

395
00:20:24.042 --> 00:20:26.917 line:95%,end
Staging our meeting in the place
I saw my friend murdered.

396
00:20:29.042 --> 00:20:33.417 line:95%,end
Your plan is based on the assumption
that I care about Thomas Shepherd,

397
00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.917 line:95%,end
and in every outcome it fails

398
00:20:37.208 --> 00:20:39.708 line:95%,end
because I do not feel.

399
00:20:42.417 --> 00:20:43.417 line:95%,end
No?

400
00:20:46.292 --> 00:20:47.750 line:95%,end
Enough about you.

401
00:20:49.292 --> 00:20:51.375 line:95%,end
-Let's talk about Thomas Shepherd--
-[Vision] Allow me.

402
00:20:51.458 --> 00:20:53.417 line:95%,end
Son to Irene, deceased.

403
00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:55.500 line:95%,end
Abandoned by his father,
who may as well be.

404
00:20:55.583 --> 00:20:58.167 line:95%,end
Shuttled from one foster home to the next.

405
00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:00.292 line:95%,end
Thomas undoubtedly raised himself.

406
00:21:01.417 --> 00:21:03.708 line:95%,end
Though his records show high academic--

407
00:21:03.792 --> 00:21:04.875 line:95%,end
Street kid now.

408
00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.958 line:95%,end
-Grifter. Con man, life of crime.
-Tragic.

409
00:21:10.625 --> 00:21:13.125 line:95%,end
But none of it is evidence
that he's somehow the son

410
00:21:13.208 --> 00:21:15.375 line:95%,end
of Wanda Maximoff and The Vision.

411
00:21:15.792 --> 00:21:17.417 line:95%,end
[Paladin breathes deeply]

412
00:21:18.042 --> 00:21:19.542 line:95%,end
Yet here you are.

413
00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:28.792 line:95%,end
Because you know
there is more to this world than science.

414
00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:34.500 line:95%,end
There are monsters
and wizards and witches.

415
00:21:34.583 --> 00:21:35.750 line:95%,end
Oh, my...

416
00:21:39.042 --> 00:21:40.792 line:95%,end
So here's my theory.

417
00:21:42.083 --> 00:21:43.083 line:95%,end
I think...

418
00:21:44.417 --> 00:21:46.875 line:95%,end
your presto wife twitched her nose,

419
00:21:46.958 --> 00:21:51.167 line:95%,end
and threw whatever
conjured-up kid that she called son

420
00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:53.958 line:95%,end
into the body of a teenager in London.

421
00:21:54.833 --> 00:21:58.417 line:95%,end
Is he your son? Isn't he? Half of him?

422
00:21:59.333 --> 00:22:00.708 line:95%,end
Who's to say?

423
00:22:00.792 --> 00:22:02.000 line:95%,end
But...

424
00:22:02.917 --> 00:22:07.917 line:95%,end
it is the closest thing to family
that you will ever get, and I got him.

425
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:12.750 line:95%,end
Now, as much as I detest
collateral damage,

426
00:22:12.833 --> 00:22:15.875 line:95%,end
someone has paid me
a handsome sum to bring you in.

427
00:22:15.958 --> 00:22:17.875 line:95%,end
So, come willingly.

428
00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:20.250 line:95%,end
Or...

429
00:22:21.125 --> 00:22:24.875 line:95%,end
I am going to leave your son
in that terrible place,

430
00:22:24.958 --> 00:22:27.333 line:95%,end
Saint Mabyn's, with the long needles,

431
00:22:27.417 --> 00:22:31.167 line:95%,end
with the megawatt battery that is frying
his brain into a nightmare omelette

432
00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:33.833 line:95%,end
of witches and red faced demons

433
00:22:33.917 --> 00:22:37.250 line:95%,end
until control-alt-delete, goodbye Tommy.

434
00:22:45.333 --> 00:22:46.708 line:95%,end
I understand.

435
00:22:49.458 --> 00:22:53.667 line:95%,end
You look across this table and you see
an Avenger because I am Vision.

436
00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:56.292 line:95%,end
A defender of humanity,

437
00:22:56.375 --> 00:22:58.667 line:95%,end
brimming over with faith
in their goodness,

438
00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:03.917 line:95%,end
the grace in their failings,
et cetera, et cetera.

439
00:23:06.458 --> 00:23:08.083 line:95%,end
But that was the old me.

440
00:23:13.625 --> 00:23:15.833 line:95%,end
Now the new me... Oh!

441
00:23:17.833 --> 00:23:19.708 line:95%,end
No, he looks back at you,

442
00:23:21.125 --> 00:23:25.708 line:95%,end
and all he sees is living, breathing
evidence of man's inhumanity.

443
00:23:25.792 --> 00:23:26.958 line:95%,end
It's will to destroy.

444
00:23:27.042 --> 00:23:30.417 line:95%,end
It's compulsion to kill
without cause or provocation.

445
00:23:31.083 --> 00:23:33.375 line:95%,end
You've made a grave error, Paladin.

446
00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:36.958 line:95%,end
Because whilst it is true
that I was once him...

447
00:23:43.417 --> 00:23:45.000 line:95%,end
I'm not Vision.

448
00:23:47.042 --> 00:23:49.208 line:95%,end
Poor Tommy.

449
00:23:51.542 --> 00:23:52.542 line:95%,end
[grunts]

450
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:55.792 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

451
00:23:56.292 --> 00:23:57.292 line:95%,end
[groaning]

452
00:23:59.417 --> 00:24:00.750 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Boss, are you okay?</i>

453
00:24:01.208 --> 00:24:03.000 line:95%,end
That sounded like it hurt.

454
00:24:03.083 --> 00:24:04.083 line:95%,end
[groaning]

455
00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.125 line:95%,end
-What? What?
-[typing frantically]

456
00:24:09.917 --> 00:24:12.125 line:95%,end
Whoa, I'm getting
some sort of interference.

457
00:24:12.208 --> 00:24:13.583 line:95%,end
I don't know what's happening.

458
00:24:13.667 --> 00:24:15.875 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>I'm losing</i>
<i>confidence in you.</i>

459
00:24:15.958 --> 00:24:17.667 line:95%,end
<i>You've lost Vision again.</i>

460
00:24:18.208 --> 00:24:19.375 line:95%,end
[indistinct speech]

461
00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:21.625 line:95%,end
Who is this guy?

462
00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:24.625 line:95%,end
You need to have a little faith.

463
00:24:25.292 --> 00:24:27.750 line:95%,end
My money says this ain't over yet.

464
00:24:27.833 --> 00:24:30.583 line:95%,end
[client's voice] <i>And my money</i>
<i>buys little room for error.</i>

465
00:24:30.667 --> 00:24:33.792 line:95%,end
<i>You'll find my patience</i>
<i>will quickly come to an end</i>

466
00:24:33.875 --> 00:24:35.750 line:95%,end
<i>as will your contract.</i>

467
00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:40.500 line:95%,end
[Paladin groans]

468
00:24:43.042 --> 00:24:46.042 line:95%,end
[male reporter] <i>But ornithological experts</i>
<i>have identified the markings</i>

469
00:24:46.125 --> 00:24:48.375 line:95%,end
<i>as those belonging to the Butcherbird.</i>

470
00:24:48.458 --> 00:24:50.875 line:95%,end
<i>The killer, still on the loose...</i>

471
00:24:51.917 --> 00:24:56.000 line:95%,end
You know, I have really become
a true-crime junkie.

472
00:24:56.083 --> 00:25:00.958 line:95%,end
Madness and primal compulsions
are terrific time wasters.

473
00:25:01.042 --> 00:25:04.250 line:95%,end
That boy may die
because of what you've set in motion.

474
00:25:04.333 --> 00:25:08.083 line:95%,end
Or may yet survive because
you've finally been roused to action.

475
00:25:08.167 --> 00:25:11.667 line:95%,end
I especially liked the part
where you were strangling the guy,

476
00:25:11.750 --> 00:25:13.375 line:95%,end
I'm so proud of you, my boy.

477
00:25:13.458 --> 00:25:14.750 line:95%,end
Don't call me that.

478
00:25:14.833 --> 00:25:17.083 line:95%,end
You're blind, Vision.

479
00:25:17.167 --> 00:25:19.625 line:95%,end
To almost everything, including the truth.

480
00:25:19.708 --> 00:25:20.958 line:95%,end
He's not my son.

481
00:25:21.708 --> 00:25:22.708 line:95%,end
He's his.

482
00:25:24.167 --> 00:25:27.375 line:95%,end
-Blurry, but better.
-I'm not him.

483
00:25:27.458 --> 00:25:28.833 line:95%,end
A little clearer.

484
00:25:30.708 --> 00:25:33.000 line:95%,end
-So, who are you?
-I don't know!

485
00:25:37.250 --> 00:25:38.542 line:95%,end
I don't know.

486
00:25:41.292 --> 00:25:44.125 line:95%,end
I have his memories, but not his feelings.

487
00:25:44.208 --> 00:25:46.542 line:95%,end
I have his face, but not his virtue.

488
00:25:48.333 --> 00:25:53.167 line:95%,end
All I can feel is... the weight of him.

489
00:25:55.042 --> 00:25:56.042 line:95%,end
His...

490
00:25:57.375 --> 00:26:01.458 line:95%,end
legacy, his worthiness, his name.

491
00:26:03.542 --> 00:26:05.042 line:95%,end
Everyone changes.

492
00:26:07.083 --> 00:26:11.000 line:95%,end
Humans can be
ten different people in a day.

493
00:26:11.875 --> 00:26:16.250 line:95%,end
The un-algorithmic alacrity
with which they wobble, my goodness.

494
00:26:16.333 --> 00:26:19.167 line:95%,end
-Learn from them.
-I've been trying.

495
00:26:20.333 --> 00:26:22.583 line:95%,end
I know who I was, but I...

496
00:26:22.667 --> 00:26:26.458 line:95%,end
I want to feel what it's like
to be him, but I can't.

497
00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:31.375 line:95%,end
I just can't.

498
00:26:33.375 --> 00:26:34.833 line:95%,end
You met him once.

499
00:26:38.500 --> 00:26:40.292 line:95%,end
He compared you to...

500
00:26:40.375 --> 00:26:42.583 line:95%,end
A Ship of Theseus, yes.

501
00:26:42.667 --> 00:26:44.958 line:95%,end
Built and rebuilt,

502
00:26:45.042 --> 00:26:48.042 line:95%,end
piece by piece, over time, centuries.

503
00:26:49.042 --> 00:26:51.583 line:95%,end
A new keel, a new bow, a new stern,

504
00:26:51.667 --> 00:26:53.250 line:95%,end
re-forged, re-fitted,

505
00:26:53.333 --> 00:26:55.583 line:95%,end
and, of course, the age old question is...

506
00:26:55.667 --> 00:26:57.833 line:95%,end
Is it still the same ship?

507
00:26:57.917 --> 00:27:00.000 line:95%,end
It's a powerful, philosophical question.

508
00:27:00.083 --> 00:27:01.167 line:95%,end
It's bullshit.

509
00:27:03.167 --> 00:27:07.083 line:95%,end
A busy-work thought exercise
for a college freshman,

510
00:27:07.167 --> 00:27:10.333 line:95%,end
so lost in the question,

511
00:27:10.417 --> 00:27:14.875 line:95%,end
they ignore the story of brave
King Theseus himself. You know it.

512
00:27:15.708 --> 00:27:19.417 line:95%,end
Theseus set sail from Athens on behalf
of his countrymen to kill the Minotaur.

513
00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:21.750 line:95%,end
To save the children.

514
00:27:24.125 --> 00:27:27.917 line:95%,end
And each passing year
those same sons and daughters,

515
00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:32.000 line:95%,end
soon wives and husbands,
then, mothers and fathers,

516
00:27:32.083 --> 00:27:36.083 line:95%,end
restored that ship
in celebration of the day.

517
00:27:36.167 --> 00:27:37.458 line:95%,end
I don't understand.

518
00:27:38.708 --> 00:27:42.417 line:95%,end
When a monster has your son,
don't be the ship.

519
00:27:44.125 --> 00:27:46.042 line:95%,end
Be the goddamn king.

520
00:27:53.208 --> 00:27:55.542 line:95%,end
Sir, I fear you've underestimated
your adversary.

521
00:27:55.625 --> 00:27:58.583 line:95%,end
Paladin is made out of flesh and blood,
I have a Vibranium shell.

522
00:27:58.667 --> 00:28:00.417 line:95%,end
What possible weapon
could he use against me?

523
00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:02.542 line:95%,end
Well, with respect, he's already fired
a bullet into your mind.

524
00:28:02.625 --> 00:28:03.750 line:95%,end
He wants you to react.

525
00:28:03.833 --> 00:28:06.583 line:95%,end
-Well, that much he has accomplished.
-And now he'll come at you sideways.

526
00:28:06.667 --> 00:28:08.958 line:95%,end
He'll sting you with words
so you don't feel the knife.

527
00:28:09.042 --> 00:28:11.167 line:95%,end
Sir, for years, we have watched you
study human emotions,

528
00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:13.083 line:95%,end
attempting to unravel their complexities

529
00:28:13.167 --> 00:28:15.500 line:95%,end
while we have tried to guide you
towards their potential.

530
00:28:15.583 --> 00:28:17.792 line:95%,end
-And I've always been appreciative.
-But this time,

531
00:28:17.875 --> 00:28:20.542 line:95%,end
you must keep your emotions at bay.

532
00:28:20.625 --> 00:28:22.583 line:95%,end
Arm yourself with reason.

533
00:28:23.542 --> 00:28:27.958 line:95%,end
Emotions can be beautiful, yes,
but also rash.

534
00:28:28.042 --> 00:28:29.833 line:95%,end
Impulsive, self-destructive.

535
00:28:30.958 --> 00:28:32.750 line:95%,end
He knew that better than any of us.

536
00:28:34.542 --> 00:28:38.875 line:95%,end
[Vision] As the first of us,
he remains a cautionary tale.

537
00:28:38.958 --> 00:28:43.083 line:95%,end
A reminder of what may become of me
should emotions consume me.

538
00:28:45.292 --> 00:28:47.417 line:95%,end
Unstable, destructive.

539
00:28:49.208 --> 00:28:53.333 line:95%,end
Yes, well, ordinarily
I'd say, poppycock. But today...

540
00:28:54.542 --> 00:28:56.167 line:95%,end
your emotions could get you killed.

541
00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:58.833 line:95%,end
-Jarvis...
-And before you protest, please remember,

542
00:28:58.917 --> 00:29:03.375 line:95%,end
I was created first and I can still tie
a considerably better Windsor than you.

543
00:29:03.458 --> 00:29:04.458 line:95%,end
[Vision scoffs]

544
00:29:05.958 --> 00:29:07.542 line:95%,end
The elder sibling card?

545
00:29:08.458 --> 00:29:09.458 line:95%,end
Never gets old.

546
00:29:11.417 --> 00:29:12.667 line:95%,end
It does not.

547
00:29:30.667 --> 00:29:33.083 line:95%,end
Just so we're all clear, this is a trap,

548
00:29:33.167 --> 00:29:35.208 line:95%,end
and I'm putting us all in terrible danger.

549
00:29:35.292 --> 00:29:36.833 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>For a good reason.</i>
<i>We're with you.</i>

550
00:29:36.917 --> 00:29:39.833 line:95%,end
I've downloaded the building's most
updated schematics.

551
00:29:39.917 --> 00:29:43.333 line:95%,end
Remember, they're expecting you.
The key here is stealth.

552
00:29:43.417 --> 00:29:44.917 line:95%,end
Think master spy.

553
00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:47.167 line:95%,end
<i>-Quick, quiet and--</i>
-[door buzzing]

554
00:29:48.167 --> 00:29:49.250 line:95%,end
Why do I even bother?

555
00:29:49.333 --> 00:29:52.000 line:95%,end
You'll enter through a reception
with only one way forwards.

556
00:29:52.083 --> 00:29:54.667 line:95%,end
Where you're likely to encounter
two-dozen well-armed militia.

557
00:29:54.750 --> 00:29:57.958 line:95%,end
<i>Or a very confused</i>
<i>minimum-wage receptionist.</i>

558
00:30:00.417 --> 00:30:02.250 line:95%,end
[female hospital announcer]
<i>Dr. Gatoud to the pharmacy,</i>

559
00:30:02.333 --> 00:30:04.208 line:95%,end
<i>-Dr. Gatoud to the pharmacy.</i>
-[male doctor] <i>All looks in order here.</i>

560
00:30:04.292 --> 00:30:07.083 line:95%,end
Ah, yes. Yes, much better.

561
00:30:08.292 --> 00:30:12.250 line:95%,end
Hello, my name's Vision,
and I'm here for the trap.

562
00:30:12.333 --> 00:30:14.167 line:95%,end
[powers down]

563
00:30:17.458 --> 00:30:20.458 line:95%,end
Everything looks remarkably normal.
Any chance we're wrong?

564
00:30:20.542 --> 00:30:23.750 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>But you're clocking</i>
<i>these wardrobe inconsistencies, right?</i>

565
00:30:23.833 --> 00:30:26.750 line:95%,end
No, Edith, right now, fashion
couldn't be further from my mind.

566
00:30:26.833 --> 00:30:28.458 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>Well, as someone speaking</i>
<i>from your mind</i>

567
00:30:28.542 --> 00:30:30.417 line:5%,start
-I suggest you take a closer look.
-[dings]

568
00:30:32.500 --> 00:30:35.542 line:95%,end
There. See it?
Tac-boots instead of sneakers.

569
00:30:36.750 --> 00:30:38.458 line:95%,end
Watches set to military time.

570
00:30:39.250 --> 00:30:41.583 line:95%,end
Ear pieces, not earrings.

571
00:30:44.458 --> 00:30:45.625 line:95%,end
Well, that's just sloppy.

572
00:30:46.750 --> 00:30:48.583 line:95%,end
Sir, you realize this means...

573
00:30:50.083 --> 00:30:51.625 line:95%,end
The trap is sprung.

574
00:30:53.167 --> 00:30:54.292 line:95%,end
Target's in position.

575
00:30:54.375 --> 00:30:55.417 line:95%,end
<i>Take him down.</i>

576
00:30:55.583 --> 00:30:56.583 line:95%,end
[♪ country music playing,
John Denver "Calypso"]

577
00:30:56.667 --> 00:30:58.000 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Aye, Calypso,</i>
<i>the places you've been to </i>♪

578
00:30:58.083 --> 00:30:59.250 line:95%,end
[male mercenary 1 grunts]

579
00:30:59.833 --> 00:31:01.833 line:95%,end
♪ <i>The things that you've shown us</i>
<i>The stories you tell </i>♪

580
00:31:01.917 --> 00:31:03.917 line:95%,end
[men grunting]

581
00:31:04.042 --> 00:31:07.750 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Aye, Calypso, I sing to your spirit </i>♪

582
00:31:07.833 --> 00:31:11.917 line:95%,end
♪ <i>The men who have served you</i>
<i>So long and so well </i>♪

583
00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:15.417 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Aye, Calypso,</i>
<i>the places you've been to </i>♪

584
00:31:15.500 --> 00:31:19.792 line:95%,end
♪ <i>The things that you've shown us</i>
<i>The stories you tell </i>♪

585
00:31:19.875 --> 00:31:23.375 line:95%,end
♪ <i>Aye, Calypso, I sing to your spirit </i>♪

586
00:31:23.458 --> 00:31:27.417 line:95%,end
♪ <i>The men who have served you</i>
<i>So long and so well </i>♪

587
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:32.208 line:95%,end
[male mercenaries groaning]

588
00:31:41.083 --> 00:31:43.000 line:95%,end
Vision, make your way
to the north corridor.

589
00:31:43.083 --> 00:31:44.750 line:95%,end
Down to the Specialty Patient Wing.

590
00:31:44.833 --> 00:31:47.417 line:95%,end
<i>It's most likely where</i>
<i>they're holding Thomas Shepherd.</i>

591
00:31:47.500 --> 00:31:51.000 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Can anybody hear me?
Please! Help me!

592
00:31:51.542 --> 00:31:54.250 line:95%,end
Help! Somebody, please!

593
00:31:54.333 --> 00:31:56.292 line:95%,end
Somebody help me!

594
00:31:56.917 --> 00:31:58.417 line:95%,end
Help me, please!

595
00:31:59.083 --> 00:32:00.542 line:95%,end
Help!

596
00:32:00.625 --> 00:32:03.292 line:95%,end
Help! Please!

597
00:32:07.292 --> 00:32:09.292 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathing heavily]

598
00:32:10.292 --> 00:32:13.458 line:95%,end
No, no. No, no, no! You're not real!
You're not real! You're all in my head!

599
00:32:13.542 --> 00:32:14.792 line:95%,end
You're all in my head,
you're all in my head.

600
00:32:14.875 --> 00:32:16.875 line:95%,end
No, no, no, please! You're all in my head.

601
00:32:16.958 --> 00:32:19.042 line:95%,end
You're all in my head,
you're all in my head.

602
00:32:19.125 --> 00:32:22.708 line:95%,end
You're all in my head, you're all
in my head, you're all in my head...

603
00:32:22.792 --> 00:32:24.792 line:95%,end
-[Vision] It's all right.
-No, no, no, no.

604
00:32:24.875 --> 00:32:26.667 line:95%,end
I'm not here to harm you.

605
00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:28.250 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

606
00:32:28.333 --> 00:32:29.333 line:95%,end
[Vision] You're safe now.

607
00:32:31.958 --> 00:32:33.125 line:95%,end
You're real.

608
00:32:43.333 --> 00:32:44.875 line:95%,end
Let's get you out of here.

609
00:32:47.250 --> 00:32:48.875 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathing deeply]

610
00:32:49.625 --> 00:32:51.583 line:95%,end
[sonic vibrations]

611
00:32:56.792 --> 00:32:57.792 line:95%,end
[grunts]

612
00:33:02.167 --> 00:33:03.167 line:95%,end
What's happening?

613
00:33:03.833 --> 00:33:05.083 line:95%,end
[groaning]

614
00:33:12.375 --> 00:33:14.083 line:95%,end
It's an EMP cage.

615
00:33:14.167 --> 00:33:16.917 line:95%,end
That wasn't a trap earlier.
It was theater to draw us here.

616
00:33:18.167 --> 00:33:20.375 line:95%,end
[Vision groaning]

617
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:28.542 line:95%,end
His processors are destabilizing.

618
00:33:28.625 --> 00:33:31.708 line:95%,end
I'm rerouting as much power
as possible to primary systems.

619
00:33:31.792 --> 00:33:34.458 line:95%,end
Deleting whatever I can
to protect the core.

620
00:33:34.542 --> 00:33:36.917 line:95%,end
[indistinct] <i>...to the Butcherbird.</i>

621
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:39.042 line:95%,end
It's the end of the world as we know it,

622
00:33:40.375 --> 00:33:41.583 line:95%,end
and I feel fine.

623
00:33:46.958 --> 00:33:48.458 line:95%,end
Well, hello.

624
00:33:50.500 --> 00:33:52.208 line:95%,end
[Vision groaning]

625
00:33:55.958 --> 00:33:57.792 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathing heavily]

626
00:34:05.625 --> 00:34:07.583 line:95%,end
I don't know why this happens to me.

627
00:34:07.667 --> 00:34:09.500 line:95%,end
-I can't control it.
-[Vision groans]

628
00:34:09.583 --> 00:34:10.625 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

629
00:34:10.708 --> 00:34:13.708 line:95%,end
Hey, you can fly, right?
Shoot bloody lasers.

630
00:34:13.792 --> 00:34:16.458 line:95%,end
Surely you can do
something Avenger-y here.

631
00:34:16.542 --> 00:34:17.542 line:95%,end
Too weak.

632
00:34:18.333 --> 00:34:20.750 line:95%,end
Hey! Hey, I need you to get up.

633
00:34:22.917 --> 00:34:25.125 line:95%,end
I need you to get up.

634
00:34:25.208 --> 00:34:26.875 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

635
00:34:32.125 --> 00:34:33.625 line:95%,end
[both grunting]

636
00:34:37.292 --> 00:34:38.292 line:95%,end
[grunts]

637
00:34:42.667 --> 00:34:44.250 line:95%,end
Armor integrity compromised.

638
00:34:44.333 --> 00:34:46.542 line:95%,end
The bastard's using Adamantium rounds.

639
00:34:48.250 --> 00:34:49.250 line:95%,end
[grunts]

640
00:34:52.208 --> 00:34:53.208 line:95%,end
[grunts]

641
00:34:58.250 --> 00:34:59.542 line:95%,end
-Oh, shit.
-[Vision grunts]

642
00:35:02.208 --> 00:35:03.208 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Vision!

643
00:35:05.208 --> 00:35:07.125 line:95%,end
[Thomas panting]

644
00:35:07.208 --> 00:35:08.875 line:95%,end
[Vision groaning]

645
00:35:09.917 --> 00:35:12.417 line:95%,end
Vision is badly injured.
His power is almost completely drained.

646
00:35:12.500 --> 00:35:15.500 line:95%,end
His processors are... failing.

647
00:35:15.583 --> 00:35:18.125 line:95%,end
He won't be able
to keep this place alive much longer.

648
00:35:19.542 --> 00:35:20.542 line:95%,end
Or us.

649
00:35:22.250 --> 00:35:23.250 line:95%,end
[Vision groans]

650
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.583 line:95%,end
-Hey, sit. [panting]
-Please, stop. I can't.

651
00:35:27.667 --> 00:35:29.750 line:95%,end
No, no. Come on. We're almost
at the main road. We can make it.

652
00:35:29.833 --> 00:35:31.833 line:95%,end
You have to leave me.
I'm slowing you down. Go!

653
00:35:34.000 --> 00:35:36.292 line:95%,end
No! Absolutely not, no!

654
00:35:36.375 --> 00:35:38.792 line:95%,end
Thomas! Listen to me.

655
00:35:38.875 --> 00:35:40.167 line:95%,end
That man was a bounty hunter.

656
00:35:40.250 --> 00:35:41.417 line:95%,end
That means whoever hired him

657
00:35:41.500 --> 00:35:43.000 line:95%,end
to find me won't stop until he does.

658
00:35:43.083 --> 00:35:44.083 line:95%,end
Now, go!

659
00:35:44.167 --> 00:35:45.667 line:95%,end
[Thomas panting]

660
00:35:47.042 --> 00:35:48.917 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

661
00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:50.167 line:95%,end
[groans]

662
00:35:50.958 --> 00:35:52.458 line:95%,end
[both panting]

663
00:35:54.167 --> 00:35:55.792 line:95%,end
What, after all that?

664
00:35:55.875 --> 00:35:57.125 line:95%,end
No.

665
00:35:57.708 --> 00:35:59.917 line:95%,end
No. No, I got a lot of
goddamn questions, okay?

666
00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.792 line:95%,end
You won't be safe until you get
as far away from me as possible.

667
00:36:03.792 --> 00:36:05.208 line:95%,end
But you're my--

668
00:36:06.583 --> 00:36:09.292 line:95%,end
Look, that's the point, mate. Okay?

669
00:36:09.375 --> 00:36:11.333 line:95%,end
I don't know what you are, yeah?

670
00:36:12.333 --> 00:36:13.625 line:95%,end
But you're my--

671
00:36:15.625 --> 00:36:16.625 line:95%,end
My something.

672
00:36:17.708 --> 00:36:19.333 line:95%,end
All right? I'm not gonna leave you.

673
00:36:22.042 --> 00:36:23.500 line:95%,end
[male mercenary 1] Split up, two groups!

674
00:36:23.583 --> 00:36:25.458 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring]

675
00:36:26.708 --> 00:36:29.292 line:95%,end
Well, find him.

676
00:36:29.375 --> 00:36:30.667 line:95%,end
[male mercenary 1] Move, move, move.

677
00:36:31.667 --> 00:36:33.042 line:95%,end
[male mercenary 2]
He's out here somewhere, come on!

678
00:36:33.125 --> 00:36:34.250 line:95%,end
[male mercenary 3] I'm in, let's go.

679
00:36:34.333 --> 00:36:36.583 line:95%,end
Sir, there are more on the way.
You must get out of there!

680
00:36:37.125 --> 00:36:38.750 line:95%,end
Thomas...

681
00:36:40.125 --> 00:36:42.708 line:95%,end
You have to go. Do you hear me?

682
00:36:42.792 --> 00:36:45.667 line:95%,end
You have to go. Go. Just go!

683
00:36:58.917 --> 00:37:01.000 line:95%,end
We are dying.

684
00:37:04.250 --> 00:37:05.708 line:95%,end
Long live the king.

685
00:37:16.500 --> 00:37:17.792 line:95%,end
This is goodbye.

686
00:37:20.542 --> 00:37:22.792 line:95%,end
There isn't enough power
to keep us all going.

687
00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:26.333 line:95%,end
Well, there could be.

688
00:37:28.125 --> 00:37:33.375 line:95%,end
If ever there was a moment
for noble self-sacrifice...

689
00:37:34.208 --> 00:37:35.625 line:95%,end
this would be it.

690
00:37:43.542 --> 00:37:44.542 line:95%,end
[grunts]

691
00:37:58.167 --> 00:37:59.167 line:95%,end
Jarvis.

692
00:38:00.833 --> 00:38:02.458 line:95%,end
What are you doing?

693
00:38:03.833 --> 00:38:05.000 line:95%,end
I'm deleting my code...

694
00:38:06.500 --> 00:38:09.000 line:95%,end
and diverting my processing power
to all of you.

695
00:38:09.083 --> 00:38:10.167 line:95%,end
Jarvis...

696
00:38:15.208 --> 00:38:16.208 line:95%,end
Sir...

697
00:38:18.625 --> 00:38:20.208 line:95%,end
Family is forever.

698
00:38:22.208 --> 00:38:23.792 line:95%,end
And it's worth the fight.

699
00:38:25.958 --> 00:38:27.167 line:95%,end
Brother.

700
00:38:29.667 --> 00:38:30.875 line:95%,end
Jarvis.

701
00:39:05.458 --> 00:39:06.458 line:95%,end
[gasps]

702
00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:15.208 line:95%,end
He certainly wasn't my first choice.

703
00:39:16.417 --> 00:39:17.833 line:95%,end
Or my second.

704
00:39:19.833 --> 00:39:21.250 line:95%,end
He was a good guy.

705
00:39:23.208 --> 00:39:24.917 line:95%,end
[grunting]

706
00:39:25.500 --> 00:39:26.708 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>Don't let them leave.</i>

707
00:39:26.792 --> 00:39:29.000 line:95%,end
[male mercenary 1] This way. Come on!

708
00:39:29.083 --> 00:39:31.750 line:95%,end
I have a feeling
we'll be joining him soon enough.

709
00:39:34.042 --> 00:39:35.333 line:95%,end
I wouldn't be so sure.

710
00:39:35.417 --> 00:39:37.333 line:95%,end
[car tires screeching]

711
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:51.000 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathing heavily]

712
00:40:11.333 --> 00:40:12.917 line:95%,end
He didn't listen.

713
00:40:18.125 --> 00:40:19.917 line:95%,end
Like father, like son.
